  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niue Direct Aid Program 2021 - 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Niue Direct Aid Program (DAP) 2021 - 2025 is a small grants program funded from Australia&apos;s aid budget. DAP projects cover a range of sectors such as education, health, water and sanitation, environmental protection, women&apos;s empowerment, gender equality, supporting people with disabilities, economic livelihoods, food security and human rights.

DAP projects engage a wide range of partners including community groups, non-government organisations, educational institutions, and local governments. It has the flexibility to work with local communities on projects that reduce poverty and achieve sustainable development consistent with Australia&apos;s national interest.

DAP sits alongside Australia&apos;s longer-term country and multilateral development strategies (see INN773 &apos;Niue Australia Development Programme 2021 - 2025&apos;). Through helping people in need, we can show Australia is a supportive and trusted partner in addressing aid challenges in partner countries.</narrative>
  </description>
